{"availability":"available","full":"nurmuhammedkanybekov/tdJamaat-v2","name":"tdJamaat-v2","description":"weekly house rankings for a Muslim community in Hungary ","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-24T09:41:10Z","updated":"2026-10-08T16:46:10Z","branch":"master","homepage":"https://tdjamaat.vercel.app","topics":["pwa","react","supabase","typescript","vercel"],"demo":"https://tdjamaat.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:40.845Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:40.845Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:40.845Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:43:40.845Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A weekly performance dashboard for a Kyrgyz Muslim community (jamaat) in Hungary, organized into houses. Each house's leaders log individual member metrics and team activity once a week; the app turns that into rankings, per-member scores, awards and trend charts everyone in the community can see. The interface is in Kyrgyz.","Rebuilt from the original tdJamaat as an independent project on a normalized data model — real houses and members instead of a JSON blob re-typed every week — with per-house authenticated logins instead of one shared password, seasons, and a full visual redesign.","Light theme, invented demo data. The site also has a black-and-gold dark theme."],"features":["Public dashboard, gated editing. Anyone in the community can open","the site and see current rankings — no login required. Entering or changing data requires signing in.","Per-house logins. Each house's leaders share one password and can","only write that house's own weekly numbers; a separate admin login manages the roster and can edit anything. Enforced by Postgres row-level security, not just hidden in the UI.","Role-scaled targets. An imam, a zam (deputy), and a regular member"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nurmuhammedkanybekov/tdJamaat-v